Copy the AOR out of the request before fill_contact() frees it.

For a reply, fill_contact() re-parses the transaction's request into tmsg to
find the UE's Contact, and then frees tmsg straight after parsing:

	cb = cscf_parse_contacts(&tmsg);
	free_sip_msg(&tmsg);
	if(!cb || (!cb->contacts)) {
	...
		if(pkg_str_dup(&aor, &cb->contacts->uri) < 0) {

cb is the parsed Contact body hanging off tmsg's headers, so free_sip_msg()
releases it (free_contact() via free_hdr_field_lst()) and both cb->contacts
and cb->contacts->uri are read from freed pkg memory. ipsec_create() runs
this on every 401 to a REGISTER. With kamailio's own pkg allocator the freed
fragment usually still holds the old bytes, so it went unnoticed; memcheck
with system malloc (-X sm) reports "Invalid read of size 8 at fill_contact"
on the 401 of a registration.

Duplicate the AOR while tmsg is still parsed, then free it, and fall back to
the Via-built AOR when no Contact gave one.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_ipsec_pcscf/cmd.c b/src/modules/ims_ipsec_pcscf/cmd.c
index 0c03ad60ba..e9b668cba9 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_ipsec_pcscf/cmd.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_ipsec_pcscf/cmd.c
@@ -346,8 +346,15 @@ static int fill_contact(
 			goto error;
 		}
 		cb = cscf_parse_contacts(&tmsg);
+		/* cb hangs off tmsg's parsed headers: copy the AOR out before
+		 * free_sip_msg() releases them */
+		if(cb && cb->contacts && pkg_str_dup(&aor, &cb->contacts->uri) < 0) {
+			LM_ERR("failed to duplicate aor\n");
+			free_sip_msg(&tmsg);
+			goto error;
+		}
 		free_sip_msg(&tmsg);
-		if(!cb || (!cb->contacts)) {
+		if(aor.s == NULL) {
 			LM_DBG("Reply No contact headers, building AOR from Via\n");
 			// Handle the messages without contacts (e.g.BYE)
 			// Build AOR as "sip:<via_host>:<via_port>"
@@ -366,11 +373,6 @@ static int fill_contact(
 			aor.len = aor_len;
 			LM_DBG("set AOR [%.*s], VIA [%d://%.*s:%d]\n", STR_FMT(&aor),
 					vb->proto, STR_FMT(&vb->host), vb->port);
-		} else {
-			if(pkg_str_dup(&aor, &cb->contacts->uri) < 0) {
-				LM_ERR("failed to duplicate aor\n");
-				goto error;
-			}
 		}
 
 		// populate CI with bare minimum
